aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: P2 (S2): "infinite" is taken as God's own goodness is unlimited in degree or perfection, as an attribute of one being in P2 and as goodness as a contrary is unbounded in extent, pervading everything so that no room is left for its opposite where infinite_good is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S3) does not follow (aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r1.sense1)
aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C1 (S3): evil = T, god_exists = T, infinite_good = F, infinite_good_2 = T
